{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nx=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']['CandidateSubmission']\nprint(json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"sources\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Sources\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"feedback\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"repair_of\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Rejected operation ID whose complete draft this submission repairs\",\n      \"title\": \"Repair Of\"\n    },\n    \"map_path\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Map Path\"\n    },\n    \"map_changes\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/UnderstandingChange\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"title\": \"Map Changes\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"reconnect_questions\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AuditQuestion\"\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Optional explicit question reconnections; changing an accepted Unit proposition still requires F2/F3\",\n      \"title\": \"Reconnect Questions\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"continue\",\n        \"pause\",\n        \"explained\",\n        \"obligation\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Action\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"candidate_id\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Candidate Id\"\n    },\n    \"parent_candidate_id\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Parent Candidate Id\"\n    },\n    \"question\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AuditQuestion\"\n    },\n    \"resume_conditions\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Resume Conditions\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"result_implications\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"propertyNames\": {\n        \"enum\": [\n          \"holds\",\n          \"violated\",\n          \"incomplete\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Result Implications\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"obligation\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ClaimDraft\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"bindings\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/BindingDraft\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Bindings\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"rationale\",\n    \"action\",\n    \"question\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"CandidateSubmission\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '20,110p' ../agent-source/run.go; sed -n '75,220p' ../agent-source/master/master.go; cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '20,110p' ../agent-source/run.go; sed -n '75,220p' ../agent-source/master/master.go; cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md\"","aggregated_output":"# File products for one audit investigation\n\nRead research.json for selected work and shared relationship navigation. A record locator names an existing JSON path, collection and exact match fields; paths are relative to the index directory unless absolute. Select matching records, then read field when present. Historical previews are navigation, not current pending work. Use artifact basis locators and graph_versions for old requirements, not the latest same-ID claim. Materials and execution IDs resolve through records in state.json. Full reviews, drafts and fixed inputs remain at their indexed paths.\n\nWhen capacity permits, supply an optional short Chinese report_title and one to three report_answer sentences in review items, leading with the measured discrepancy and actual observation. State decisive applicability once and keep open disputes visible; leave repeated execution detail and wider exclusions in the scoped records. Keep English semantic reasoning; actual verdicts and measurements prevail. Omission never blocks work or warrants a translation turn.\n\nWrite a complete submission.json using submission.schema.json and product-schemas.json. Cite authorized captured ranges. Follow next_objective and the analysis guide for core_overview readiness; a usable map and first Candidate may share a submission.\n\nWhen repairing a rejected product, set repair_of to its operation_id and submit the whole product. Diagnostics retain ownership: reconsider=submission calls for product repair; reconsider=research_decision requires a different research action, not field repair of an unauthorized stop. Repeated errors may pause only the draft, never unrelated questions.\n\n- continue / pause / explained / obligation: select candidate_id or fork using parent_candidate_id, with a complete current question. Sourced feedback may refine the discriminator before its first obligation; later requirement/scope changes use F2/F3. A fork explains holds/violated/incomplete effects on its parent. Pause supplies resume_conditions; explained cites the protective mechanism. Obligation supplies one attributed claim and source bindings. A complete check may be combined now, or constructed later.\n- check / revise_check: select unit_id (or its Candidate alias), or create an obligation through candidate. Supply plan_path, draft-source harness_path and optional destination-to-draft files; plan.harness.execution_package may select one Go package or Rust crate for this check. Metadata source/files stay empty; the controller fixes executable bytes and adapter support. Never replace target code or dependencies. Revisions name previous_check_id. Driver legality repairs name repair_issue_ids and explain changed inputs and sources; reference every removed conflict's exact issue. Changed executed checker encoding uses encoding_revision.\n- research: submit substantive feedback alone with acquired source or retained execution ref_ids, or a complete partial map_path, additive graph_path or scope_path. Feedback alone needs no Candidate or usable overview and creates no map version or Evidence. An identical adjacent pure handoff on unchanged research receives duplicate_of: accepted without new knowledge; continue useful investigation, not rewording. A map may accompany one graph/scope operation. semantic_revision supplies an attributed F2/F3 feedback_path for an existing unit_id and may carry a map. Graph additions cannot invent unowned executable Units.\n- review: select artifact_id; omitted item target_id inherits it. Carries feedback, not a map. Use review_contracts/review_questions: Direct Check requires checker_correspondence; other aspects are optional unless resolving an issue of that aspect. revision_needed names challenged_components. Resolve exact issue_ids using acquired Material source_ids, a concise answer and retained evidence_ids when relevant. For supplied conditions, use condition_dispositions with exact condition_id, sources and applicability; current_judgment remains unresolved. Unchanged sources and reasoning can be referenced, not recopied. The review guide defines semantic criteria. Candidate applicability review creates no execution Evidence.\n- explore: submit a question, draft-source harness_path, optional files and optional execution_package with the same meaning as Harness.execution_package. Clean-copy output guides construction without property Evidence.\n- stop: candidate/family/focus release local work; unfinished Units and disputes remain. A local tool/resource gap supplies resume_conditions. Open runs reject scope=run: continue with research, exploration or another Candidate within remaining authorization. Only a preconfigured finite directed_question may end with run/bounded_completed after its task is disposed; cite the explained, closed or checked Candidate. Cancellation, permission/service failure and exhausted time/calls are controller events, never submission authority.\n\nFor Go, omit execution_package to retain the run default package and main-file destination. An explicit local directory selects that package and places the primary file there using the configured basename. Helpers in files remain relative to the workspace root. The controller fixes the effective package and bytes before execution; it runs Go directly in a clean copy, without a root launcher. Select only one existing package in the captured module; paths, patterns, nested modules, workspaces and dependency overrides cannot expand authorization. Python does not support this override.\n\nFor Rust, execution_package selects one captured crate directory and tests/<configured basename>.rs, with workspace-relative helpers. Consult research.build_inputs for the fixed workspace lock, tools, metadata feature resolution and selected-test compilation record. Original manifests and dev-dependencies determine effective features; no extra feature flags are added. The controller prepares missing locks once, builds a neutral integration seed, removes the selected package outputs through Cargo, and gives each action a private seed copy. Each current harness is built and run with --locked --offline; preparation consumes the run deadline and cannot supply observations. Never replace manifests, locks, build scripts or tool configuration. Tree-sitter anchors establish acquired declarations, not active cfg branches, macro expansion or private-state reachability.\n\nA formal question names one principal fact_ids entry, lifecycle, direct behavior_ids, sourced A1/A2 relationship, contexts, event_paths, importance and trigger_rationale. supporting_behavior_ids maps distinct Behavior IDs to their causal role. audit_spec_version may be omitted for the current basis. A map file's version is its accepted base (1 initially); the controller assigns resulting versions, including questions in combined products and F2/F3 patches. Do not guess current+1. Unchanged Candidates retain their historical basis. A supporting-layer question cites its actual consumer or core relationship and declares the supported A1/A2 activity; a local storage obligation need not become a whole-cluster consequence. If that relationship lacks sources, investigate or retain feedback instead of inventing a core label.\n\nThe controller derives actual map differences and reverse indexes. map_changes explains modified/removed objects and new producers or consumers of an existing principal Fact, with impact (clarification/meaning/dependency), acquired source_ids and rationale. Use one preserves explanation for unchanged requirements, dependencies and observation scope, or challenges mapping saved Candidate IDs to specific disputed premises. A corrected principal Fact requires a challenge; clarification cannot disguise identity/context/edge changes or removal. Independent additions need no invented revision and may still challenge a prior interpretation.\n\nCoherent knowledge and its issues are accepted together; unaffected checks retain their basis. reconnect_questions updates explicitly selected questions. ScopeUpdate/F3 expands dependencies under its existing write rules; changed normative or fault/configuration applicability uses F2. No-op maps create no version.\n\nFor every feedback shape, including one accompanying a map, Candidate or review, ref_ids directly includes each saved CheckRun whose execution it explains, alongside relevant Candidate, Behavior, Fact, surface:<entry_point> and Material IDs. Obtain execution IDs from research.json.explorations[*].executions[*].check_id or the exact records locator, not operation/plan IDs or prose. Explaining only a repaired execution references only that run; a joint explanation references both failure and repair and distinguishes their observations. Shared sources, Behavior or harness names do not associate executions. Source-only answers need no execution reference. Map/map_changes source_ids remain Material references. understanding records learning, not a map change; use the guide's natural handoff. question_updates revises Candidate unknowns/resume_conditions with sources, retaining requirements and counterevidence. Historical remaining is then-remaining; current execution/review records remain authoritative.\n\nClaim/Scope owns requirement and applicability; Harness legality records this history and caller duties. Use the experiments reference for predicate correspondence, observation synchronization, prerequisite waits and cleanup responsibility during construction and review. Unreached setup retains its observation and calls for minimal repair preserving the discriminator. claim.concern classifies responsibility, not confidence.\n\nOptional preflight: run validation.command followed by the draft-relative filename in an existing Codex tool call. It shares acceptance preparation, writes no accepted state and executes no target; formal submission rechecks fixed bytes and current state without a preflight ticket. capacity is the current budget snapshot: new_obligation is an entry capability, not a complete check/review budget; remaining.agent_calls counts future turns, not local work in this running turn. A reliable receipt fixes only declared product files before deadline handling; saved bytes are not acceptance or Evidence. Without it, drafts remain unsubmitted. While time remains, an understood exploration answer may use feedback-only research under the same reference rule, retaining conditions, actual observations and remaining responsibility/history/endpoint questions. It need not wait for a map, Candidate or obligation to pass preflight. Keep rejected larger drafts and diagnostics separate; the small product neither repairs nor partially accepts them. Combine products when ready; no mandatory feedback turn or new deadline threshold. Natural expiry needs no closing submission.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"A concrete discrepancy merits investigation: `handleAccept` records the ballot and dependency attributes and sends an acknowledgement, but does not set the instance status to `ACCEPTED`. Recovery uses that status to choose what to preserve. I’ll retain this as a sourced question; a legal message history and applicable preservation duty still need validation.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_map.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\ndef src(i,f,a,b):\n sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind='code_observation'));return i\nsrc('M-init','epaxos/epaxos.go',31,197)\nsrc('M-dispatch','epaxos/epaxos.go',278,433)\nsrc('M-ballot','epaxos/epaxos.go',435,451)\nsrc('M-send','epaxos/epaxos.go',469,611)\nsrc('M-attrs','epaxos/epaxos.go',619,722)\nsrc('M-phase1','epaxos/epaxos.go',724,972)\nsrc('M-accept','epaxos/epaxos.go',974,1064)\nsrc('M-commit','epaxos/epaxos.go',1066,1125)\nsrc('M-recovery','epaxos/epaxos.go',1127,1314)\nsrc('M-try','epaxos/epaxos.go',1316,1485)\nsrc('M-default','epaxos/epaxos.go',1508,1529)\nsrc('M-store','epaxos/epaxos.go',199,236)\nsrc('M-exec','epaxos/exec.go',25,172)\nsrc('M-replica','replica/replica.go',63,171)\nsrc('M-wire','replica/replica.go',215,262)\nsrc('M-listener','replica/replica.go',416,521)\nsrc('M-run','run.go',23,68)\nsrc('M-master','master/master.go',75,185)\nsrc('M-defs','epaxos/defs.go',13,110)\nsrc('M-state','state/state.go',85,170)\nbs=[]\ndef beh(i,a,t,ss,**kw):\n b=dict(id=i,primary_activity=a,execution_owner='EPaxos Replica.run serialized handler loop',protocol_context='Fixed replica set; instance identified by origin replica and instance number; per-instance ballot',trigger=t,source_ids=ss);b.update(kw);bs.append(b)\nbeh('B-form','A1','Client proposal or PreAccept/PreAcceptReply dispatch',['M-phase1','M-attrs','M-send','M-defs'],writes=['Owner batches requests and allocates an instance in its row. startPhase1 computes key-indexed dependencies and installs PREACCEPTED plus fresh bookkeeping.','Follower rejects lower ballots; for status below ACCEPTED it records commands, updated attributes, ballot/value ballot and PREACCEPTED or PREACCEPTED_EQ.','Replies matching lastTriedBallot and a preaccepted bookkeeping status increment support and merge attributes; higher value ballots replace selected attributes/status.'],important_branches=['Fast decision requires FastQuorumSize()-1 replies, allEqual, committed-dependency condition for N>7, and initial ballot. Equality is skipped for N<=3 with thriftiness.','At the same threshold without fast precondition, coordinator installs ACCEPTED and broadcasts Accept.','For existing ACCEPTED-or-later state, PreAccept only fills missing commands; it indexes the command write by LeaderId, while reading the instance by Replica.'],external_effects=['Conditional metadata/command persistence and sync, PreAccept replies, Accept or Commit broadcasts, early client replies only if Dreply is false.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-record'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-record'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Ballot guards decide which requests/replies can affect formation.','A5':'A fast decision makes commands eligible for dependency execution.'})\nbeh('B-accept','A1','Accept or AcceptReply dispatch',['M-accept','M-send'],implementation_guards=['Follower rejects lower ballots and does not alter COMMITTED/EXECUTED records.','Coordinator requires bookkeeping ACCEPTED and reply ballot exactly lastTriedBallot.'],writes=['For an eligible Accept, follower assigns Deps, Seq, bal and vbal but leaves Status unchanged.','Coordinator increments acceptOKs; acceptOKs+1>N/2 sets bookkeeping and instance COMMITTED.'],external_effects=['Follower records metadata, syncs and replies with its current ballot. Coordinator commits, propagates and conditionally replies to clients.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-record'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-record'],unknowns=['Does preservation of an acknowledged Accept require an ACCEPTED status visible to subsequent Prepare and PreAccept processing?'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'The retained follower status and vbal are later exported in PrepareReply.'})\nbeh('B-context','A2','Recovery request or Prepare/PrepareReply dispatch',['M-recovery','M-ballot','M-default','M-commit'],writes=['Recovery retains pending client proposals, snapshots current value information into new bookkeeping, selects ballot and appends a self PrepareReply after overwriting local bal and vbal.','Prepare raises bal for a higher request, retaining vbal and value/status, then replies.','Matching prepare replies accumulate until SlowQuorumSize. Highest VBallot with last-on-tie selection supplies value/status. Recovery branches on COMMITTED, ACCEPTED, or preaccepted counts/equality/leader participation; otherwise restarts phase1, using NOOP for absent commands.'],important_branches=['Complete committed commands suppress recovery initiation. Selected committed state is installed without a Commit broadcast in this handler.','Old or mismatching prepare replies are rejected by preparing/ballot checks. New recovery bookkeeping resets old counters.','makeBallot uses replica identity, N, and only when IsLeader is true advances against maxRecvBallot. BeTheLeader sets IsLeader true; no revocation is shown.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-record'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-record'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Recovered status selects Accept versus renewed PreAccept, directly constraining subsequent decision formation.','A7':'Recovery carries existing client proposals into restarted phase1.'})\nbeh('B-commit','A1','Commit dispatch',['M-commit','M-attrs'],implementation_guards=['Ignore already committed/executed instances and commits below inst.bal.'],writes=['Install command, sequence, dependencies, bal/vbal and COMMITTED. Update conflict indexes and contiguous committed prefix.'],external_effects=['Record commands/metadata without local sync. A NOOP for the local row can requeue pending proposals.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-record'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-record'],cross_activity_effects={'A5':'Creates committed records consumed by execution.'})\nbeh('B-recover-trigger','A3','Execution scan encounters missing/uncommitted/commandless record',['M-dispatch'],execution_owner='executeCommands goroutine, then Replica.run',writes=['Track problematic instance and accumulated sleep quantum per row.'],external_effects=['After COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD accounting, enqueue instance IDs through instancesToRecover for recovery; normal execution retries scanning.'],async_boundaries=['Execution reads shared instance records while handler loop updates them; full memory-synchronization analysis remains open.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Queued recovery starts per-instance authority acquisition.'})\nbeh('B-execute','A5','executeCommands scan of committed record',['M-exec','M-dispatch','M-state'],execution_owner='executeCommands goroutine / Exec',implementation_guards=['Require COMMITTED status and available commands; dependency traversal returns false on unavailable or uncommitted dependencies.'],writes=['Tarjan traversal orders strongly connected components by sequence, replica ID, then proposeTime. Executes commands and marks records EXECUTED. Advances contiguous ExecedUpTo in scanner.'],external_effects=['With Dreply and local client proposals, execute and reply with result. Otherwise apply PUT; NONE does no application work.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-record'],produces_fact_ids=['F-record'],cross_activity_effects={'A7':'Execution supplies deferred client results.'})\nbeh('B-config','A4','Replica construction and peer connections',['M-replica','M-run','M-master','M-init'],execution_owner='Launcher, master and replica networking',protocol_context='Static registered node list and configured fault count',writes=['N derives from node list, F from configured address count. EPaxos construction forces Thrifty=true, LRead=false, Dreply defaults true; launcher disables durability.'],external_effects=['Master invokes BeTheLeader initially and after detected leader RPC failure. Peer Alive flags gate sends; listener failure marks a peer not alive.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'FastQuorumSize is F+(F+1)/2; SlowQuorumSize is (N+1)/2; Accept threshold uses N/2.','A2':'Master designation controls ballot retry behavior, not exclusive proposal admission.'})\nbeh('B-storage','A6','Metadata/command record and sync calls',['M-store','M-replica','M-run'],execution_owner='Handler caller',protocol_context='Optional Durable mode; off in launcher',writes=['Metadata writes bal and then vbal into the same first four bytes, followed by status, sequence and dependencies. Commands are serialized separately.'],important_branches=['All persistence helpers return when Durable=false. StableStore starts nil; restart reconstruction has not been located.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'A durable promise/recovery contract would depend on initialization, format and replay not yet established.'})\nbeh('B-client','A7','Client PROPOSE decode and reply serialization',['M-listener','M-wire','M-phase1','M-exec'],execution_owner='clientListener, delayed proposal delivery, handler and execution goroutines',protocol_context='Client CommandId and timestamp travel with local pending proposals',external_effects=['PROPOSE enters ProposeChan via delay helper; handler batches it; Dreply defaults true and execution sends result.'],unknowns=['Caller retry policy and deduplication contract remain unread; handlePropose explicitly leaves client retries as TODO.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Batched client commands start local-row instances.'})\nfact=dict(id='F-record',meaning='The local instance record carries its current command/attribute tuple, status, promise ballot and value ballot; these fields are what Prepare exports and formation/execution interprets. This does not assert that every acknowledgement establishes ACCEPTED or that the tuple is chosen.',identity={'replica':'Origin row','instance':'Slot in that row','observer':'Replica holding the record'},validity_context='In-memory snapshot at a serialized handler boundary; later protocol handlers may replace fields. Execution concurrently consumes and marks records.',representation=['Instance.Cmds','Instance.Seq','Instance.Deps','Instance.Status','Instance.bal','Instance.vbal'],durability='Conditional helpers exist; launcher disables Durable. No crash-restart claim established.',recovery='PrepareReply exports this tuple; recovery selects by VBallot and uses status to choose continuation.',source_ids=['M-phase1','M-accept','M-commit','M-recovery','M-exec'],unknowns=['Whether follower Accept acknowledgement preserves the support classification needed across recovery.'])\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nactivities=[]\nfor a,role in roles.items():\n own=[b for b in bs if b['primary_activity']==a]\n activities.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=role['relation'],realization_summary=' '.join(b['trigger']+'.' for b in own),entry_points=[b['id'] for b in own],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(s for b in own for s in b['source_ids']))))\ndef path(text,ids,ss):return dict(explanation=text,behavior_ids=ids,fact_ids=['F-record'],source_ids=ss)\nmap_=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured EPaxos implementation plus in-repository replica transport, static master configuration, state execution and client admission. Other protocol packages are outside this initial map.',protocol_contexts=['Per-origin instance rows and ballots; fixed membership; thriftiness enabled by constructor'],external_interfaces=['TCP typed peer RPCs','Client PROPOSE/ProposeReplyTS','Master registration and BeTheLeader RPC'],source_ids=['M-init','M-run','M-replica','M-listener']),activities=activities,behaviors=bs,facts=[fact],surfaces=[],core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=path('A1: A client proposal is batched by its receiving replica into a local-row instance. Conflict indexes supply sequence/dependencies; thriftiness selects a preferred live peer subset. PreAccept replies are filtered by attempted ballot and phase, then counted/merged. Fast conditions commit directly; otherwise Accept replies at matching ballot establish the coordinator commit threshold. Commit broadcasts carry commands and attributes. Recipients install guarded committed records. Dependency/SCC execution waits for prerequisite commands and committed status, applies ordered operations and answers deferred clients.',['B-form','B-accept','B-commit','B-execute','B-client','B-config'],['M-phase1','M-accept','M-send','M-commit','M-exec','M-replica']),context=path('A2: Authority is per instance, not exclusive global proposal leadership. Initial ballots equal origin replica ID. Recovery resets bookkeeping while retaining client proposals/value context, selects a ballot, adds a self reply and sends Prepare. Acceptors raise their promise and export prior value ballot/status. The recovering coordinator collects matching replies and selects a highest-value-ballot tuple before committing locally, accepting or restarting phase1. Lower-ballot requests and nonmatching replies are guarded. Complete committed records skip recovery. Master designation affects higher-ballot retry but does not stop other replicas proposing.',['B-context','B-recover-trigger','B-config'],['M-recovery','M-ballot','M-commit','M-master','M-dispatch']),connection=path('A1/A2 connection: The record status and value ballot exported by Prepare determine whether earlier formation support constrains the new attempt as committed, accepted or merely preaccepted. Reset bookkeeping discards old counts; phase and ballot checks constrain delayed replies. Accepted/committed follower guards limit new PreAccept modifications, while delayed Commit is rejected below a newer promise. Pending local client proposals survive recovery and may be reproposed after NOOP. Execution later consumes the selected record, so retention of support classification matters independently of client visibility.',['B-form','B-accept','B-context','B-commit','B-execute'],['M-phase1','M-accept','M-recovery','M-commit','M-exec']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Follower Accept leaves Status unchanged; investigate preservation through Prepare.','Prepare selection overwrites equal-VBallot tuples in reply order; recoverer also rewrites self vbal before exporting it.','TryPreAccept recovery subcase has duplicate condition after the prior branch; deeper reachability remains open.','Transport queues per message asynchronously; legal dispatch histories and shared-memory observations need question-specific review.','Fault/restart and client retry contracts remain incomplete.'],rationale='Representative formation, authority transition, old-work guards and consumption are traced with source-backed unresolved local discrepancies; no correctness or coverage claim.'))\nfor ep,reason,ss in [('recordInstanceMetadata','bal and vbal overwrite the same bytes; durable initialization/replay contract is unresolved.',['M-store']),('handleTryPreAccept','Branch selection duplicates subcase 3 condition for subcase 4; determine actual reachability before testing inner handlers.',['M-recovery','M-try']),('updateAttributes','Batch loop breaks at the first newly enlarged per-row dependency; later commands may require a greater dependency. Compare with actual command conflict responsibility.',['M-attrs','M-state']),('handlePreAccept','Missing command fill indexes LeaderId rather than origin Replica; legal recovery reachability remains unresolved.',['M-phase1']),('nodeArray.Less','Tie-break uses local proposeTime for same replica and sequence; determine whether legal SCC histories can reach that tie.',['M-exec'])]:\n map_['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point=ep,disposition='deferred',reason=reason,source_ids=ss,high_consequence=True))\nquestion=dict(question='Does acknowledging an eligible Accept while retaining a preaccepted or NONE status lose the accepted-support classification that later Prepare and recovery continuation require?',importance='If prior accepted support is reinterpreted as absent or merely preaccepted, recovery could form a decision inconsistent with earlier support. No such decision history is yet demonstrated.',source_ids=['M-accept','M-recovery','M-phase1','M-defs'],participan